  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Syed Maideen Ashik Ali vs / on 10 December, 2024 W.P.(Md) No. Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated: 10.12.2024 Coram: The Honourable Mr.Justice K.Kumaresh Babu W.P.(Md) No.12599 of 2017 and W.M.P.(Md) Nos.9713 and 13661 of 2017 1.Syed Maideen Ashik Ali 2.Mohamed Musthafa Alameen 3.Syed Jalaludeen 4.Mohamed Sahul Hameed ... Petitioners /vs./ 1.The District Revenue Officer cum Additional District Magistrate, Tirunelveli District. 2.The Food Safety Officer, Tenkasi (Town), Tirunelveli District. ... Respondents PRAYER: Writ Petition filed under Article 226 of the Constitution of In issuance of Writ of Certiorari, calling for the records relating to the order passed by the 1st Respondent/The District Revenue Officer Cum/Add 1/4 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis W.P.(MD) District Magistrate, Tirunelveli District in C.C.No.22/2015 dated 15.04 quash the same. For Petitioners : Mr.AR.Jeya Rhuthran For Respondents : Mr.R.Suresh Kumar Additional Government Pleader Syed Maideen Ashik Ali vs / on 10 December, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/45506253/ 1 ORDER",
    "facts": "The writ petition had been filed challenging the order of the first respondent under the provisions of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. 2. When the writ petition was filed, the Food Safety Appellate Tribunal was not constituted, but however as of today, the same is functional.",
    "arguments": ""
